      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 19.71,
      "answer": "Tracking tokens in the NAVAS platform are used to pay for GPS tracking based on time. Customers can choose to pay by the hour, day, or month, allowing them to only pay when their assets are active. This model supports pause and resume functions, making it flexible for different usage patterns. \n\nTokens are categorized into different classes, such as time tokens for tracking uptime, data tokens for parameter visibility, and event tokens for discrete incidents, among others. This standardization ensures consistency across products and markets.\n\nIf you need more specific information or assistance, I can connect you with someone who can help further.",
