      "answer": "VEBA is a system that introduces marketplace behaviors for asset management. It involves asset listings, booking approvals, conflict alerts, and payments. VEBA requires real-time availability, booking idle assets, canceling or rescheduling, and conflict alerts. It also includes features like owner approval or rejection of bookings and usage history for scheduling maintenance.\n\nVEBA's activity flows cover passenger booking, driver fatigue alert handling, aggregator commission processing, document upload and verification, and token usage and deduction. It mandates KYC verification, token deduction audits, commission rules, and enforcement for payment disputes.\n\nIf you need more detailed information or specific assistance with VEBA, I can connect you with someone who can help further.",
